# 🧬 Hierarchy-aware Medication Recommendation

[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10+-blue)](https://python.org)
[![PyTorch](https://img.shields.io/badge/PyTorch-2.0+-red)](https://pytorch.org)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green)](LICENSE)

> **Integrating patient EHR data with drug molecular structure for ATC hierarchy-aware multi-label drug recommendation.**  
> *Improves accuracy, interpretability, and clinical consistency through multimodal fusion and hierarchical modeling.*

---

## 📌 You need to know first!

| Branch | Purpose |
|:-------|:--------|
| `main` | Full implementation with hierarchical ATC prediction + drug molecular fusion |
| `archived` | Legacy version for reproducing paper results |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which branch to use?**
> - Use this branch (`main`) for learning and using the code
> - Use the [archived branch](https://github.com/ycq091044/SafeDrug/tree/archived) to reproduce paper results

> [!NOTE]
> **Implementation differences from paper:**
> 1. Drug SMILES strings: paper's crawling method missed many molecules; current branch uses **DrugBank method** for more comprehensive coverage
> 2. Data preprocessing script differs → output statistics may vary from paper

---

## ✨ Highlights

| Feature | Description |
|:--------|:------------|
| 🏥 **Hierarchical ATC prediction** | L1 → L2 → L3 → L4 |
| 💊 **Cross-attention drug knowledge fusion** | Multimodal integration |
| ⚖️ **4-layer defense for class imbalance** | Robust handling |
| 🎯 **Performance** | F1 = 0.70, Jaccard = 0.55 on MIMIC-III |

---

## 📦 Requirements

```bash
Python 3.10+
PyTorch 2.0+
CUDA 11.8+ (for GPU training)
```

---

## 📁 Data Preparation

### File Structure

```
data/
└── mimic3/
    ├── raw/                    # Raw MIMIC-III data
    │   ├── PRESCRIPTIONS.csv
    │   ├── DIAGNOSES_ICD.csv
    │   └── PROCEDURES_ICD.csv
    ├── auxiliary/              # Auxiliary files
    │   ├── drug-DDI.csv       # From GAMENet
    │   ├── drug-atc.csv       # From GAMENet
    │   └── ndc2rxcui.txt      # NDC to RXCUI mapping
    └── l_data/                 # Preprocessed data (generated)
        ├── train_atc_hierarchy2.json
        ├── val_atc_hierarchy2.json
        ├── test_atc_hierarchy2.json
        └── drug_embeddings.pt
```

### Download Instructions

1. **MIMIC-III Dataset**  
   Apply for access at [MIMIC-III](https://mimic.mit.edu/) and place files in `data/mimic3/raw/`

2. **Auxiliary Files**  
   Download from [GAMENet](https://github.com/sjy1203/GAMENet):
   - `drug-DDI.csv`
   - `drug-atc.csv`
   - `ndc2rxcui.txt` (rename from `ndc2rxnorm_mapping.csv`)

3. **Preprocess**

```bash
cd data/mimic3
python construction.py
```

> [!TIP]
> Preprocessing will generate the `l_data/` folder automatically.

---

## 🚀 Running

### Training

```bash
bash experiment/llm_cls.bash
```

**Key hyperparameters** (set in `experiment/llm_cls.bash`):

| Parameter | Value |
|:----------|:------|
| `MAX_SOURCE_LENGTH` | 2048 |
| `MAX_TARGET_LENGTH` | 196 |
| `BATCH_SIZE` | 4 |
| `LEARNING_RATE` | 3e-4 |
| `LORA_RANK` | 8 |

### Evaluation

```bash
python batch_evaluate_checkpoints.py
```

> [!NOTE]
> Batch evaluation for multiple checkpoints.

---

## 📊 Results

| Metric | Score |
|:-------|:------|
| **F1** | 0.70 |
| **Jaccard** | 0.55 |

*Evaluated on MIMIC-III dataset.*

